WEBVTT

00:00:00.675 --> 00:00:34.648
The Fisherman and His Soul by Oscar Wilde Copyright Black Cat Publishing Chapter 1 The Mermaid Every evening, the Fisherman went out fishing He sometimes sold his fish at the market.

00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:40.300
Sometimes he did not catch many fish and he could not sell them.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.312
One evening, his net was very heavy.

00:00:44.372 --> 00:00:51.394
He laughed and said, Did I catch all the fish in the sea?

00:00:51.454 --> 00:00:55.276
Or did I catch some horrible monster?

00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:57.956
I will give it to the queen.

00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:59.934
She will be happy.

00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:03.942
He pulled and pulled the heavy net.

00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:08.063
Finally, he pulled the net next to the boat.

00:01:08.123 --> 00:01:13.644
But there were no fish in it, and there was no monster.

00:01:13.704 --> 00:01:16.865
There was only a little mermaid.

00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:19.136
She was asleep.

00:01:19.196 --> 00:01:22.637
Her hair was yellow like gold.

00:01:22.697 --> 00:01:26.488
Her body was white like ivory.

00:01:26.548 --> 00:01:34.003
Her tail like silver and pearl, and her ears like seashells.

00:01:34.062 --> 00:01:37.065
She was very beautiful.

00:01:37.124 --> 00:01:41.018
The fisherman pulled the net closer to the boat.

00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:43.098
He embraced her.

00:01:43.158 --> 00:01:47.292
When he touched her, she screamed.

00:01:47.352 --> 00:01:55.646
She could not escape, so she began to cry and said, Please let me go.

00:01:55.706 --> 00:01:59.175
I am the only daughter of the king of the sea.

00:01:59.235 --> 00:02:03.256
My father is very old and alone."

00:02:03.316 --> 00:02:06.398
But the fisherman answered her.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:11.570
I will let you go, but you must make me a promise.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.452
I will call you and you will come and sing to me.

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:21.164
The fish love the songs of the people of the sea.

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:25.236
You will sing and my nets will be full.

00:02:25.296 --> 00:02:26.889
I promise!

00:02:26.949 --> 00:02:29.070
Please let me go!"

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:30.952
cried the mermaid.

00:02:31.011 --> 00:02:34.134
Yes, I will let you go.

00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:35.986
said the fisherman.

00:02:36.046 --> 00:02:40.368
So she promised him, and he let her go.

00:02:40.428 --> 00:02:44.662
She went back into the sea and trembled.

00:02:44.722 --> 00:02:48.094
She felt a strange fear.

00:02:48.154 --> 00:02:54.475
Every evening the young fisherman went fishing and called the mermaid.

00:02:54.535 --> 00:02:58.014
She came and sang to him.

00:02:58.074 --> 00:03:01.597
The dolphins swam round and round her.

00:03:01.656 --> 00:03:05.480
The seagulls were in the sky above her head.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:12.085
She sang a marvellous song of the tritons, the men with long green beards.

00:03:12.144 --> 00:03:16.468
She sang of the gardens of the sea with their corals.

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:20.212
Hear the fish swim like silver birds.

00:03:20.272 --> 00:03:31.250
She sang of the big whales from the cold north seas and of the dead sailors in their ships at the bottom of the sea.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.712
She sang of the little children.

00:03:34.772 --> 00:03:39.264
They ride on the backs of the dolphins and laugh.

00:03:39.324 --> 00:03:44.446
When she sang, the tuna fish came to listen to her.

00:03:44.506 --> 00:03:49.040
The young fisherman then caught many of them.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:56.946
When his boat was full of fish, the mermaid smiled at him and swam away.

00:03:57.005 --> 00:04:00.178
But she never came near him.

00:04:00.238 --> 00:04:06.272
When he tried to catch her, she went into the water like a seal.

00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:11.006
Each day her voice became sweeter to his ears.

00:04:11.066 --> 00:04:16.179
Soon he forgot his nets and listened to her song.

00:04:16.238 --> 00:04:20.413
He listened to her until the moon came.

00:04:20.473 --> 00:04:29.830
One evening he called her and said, Little Mermaid, marry me because I love you.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:41.378
But the little mermaid said, you have a human soul, send away your soul, and then I can love you.

00:04:41.438 --> 00:04:46.586
The young fisherman thought, Why do I need my soul?

00:04:46.646 --> 00:04:48.166
I cannot see it.

00:04:48.226 --> 00:04:49.847
I cannot touch it.

00:04:49.907 --> 00:04:51.968
I do not know it.

00:04:52.028 --> 00:04:56.709
Of course, I will send it away and I will be very happy.

00:04:56.769 --> 00:05:00.261
He stood up in his boat and cried.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.242
I will send my soul away.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:09.954
You will be my wife and you will show me all the things you sing about.

00:05:10.014 --> 00:05:13.822
We will be together forever.

00:05:13.882 --> 00:05:19.232
The little mermaid laughed because she was very happy.

00:05:19.292 --> 00:05:22.373
But how can I send my soul away?

00:05:22.433 --> 00:05:24.784
cried the young fisherman.

00:05:24.844 --> 00:05:29.385
I do not know, said the little mermaid.

00:05:29.445 --> 00:05:34.246
The people of the sea have no souls.

00:05:34.306 --> 00:05:43.364
Early the next morning, the fisherman went to the priest's house and knocked on his door.

00:05:43.424 --> 00:05:52.792
The priest looked out of the window and saw the fisherman and said, Come in.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:57.384
The young fisherman entered and cried to the priest.

00:05:57.444 --> 00:06:01.086
Father, I am in love with a mermaid.

00:06:01.146 --> 00:06:05.168
I cannot marry her because I have a soul.

00:06:05.228 --> 00:06:08.270
How can I send my soul away?

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.462
I really do not need it.

00:06:11.522 --> 00:06:14.571
Why is my soul important?

00:06:14.631 --> 00:06:16.680
I cannot see it.

00:06:16.739 --> 00:06:18.750
I cannot touch it.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.041
I do not know it.

00:06:21.101 --> 00:06:25.203
The priest answered, Are you mad?

00:06:25.262 --> 00:06:28.684
God gave you your soul.

00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:31.754
It is very precious.

00:06:31.814 --> 00:06:36.766
It is as precious as all the gold in the world.

00:06:36.826 --> 00:06:41.828
So my son, do not think about this anymore.

00:06:41.888 --> 00:06:44.888
It is the worst sin.

00:06:44.948 --> 00:06:48.799
The people of the sea are lost creatures.

00:06:48.858 --> 00:06:52.252
They are like the beasts of the field.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:55.786
They do not know what is right and wrong.

00:06:55.845 --> 00:06:58.758
God didn't die for them.

00:06:58.778 --> 00:07:12.440
The young fisherman began to cry and said, Father, the phones live in the forest and are happy.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:17.161
The mermaids sit on the rocks with their gold harps.

00:07:17.221 --> 00:07:19.642
I want to be like them.

00:07:19.702 --> 00:07:22.343
Why is my soul important?

00:07:22.402 --> 00:07:28.184
I have a soul, but I cannot have the mermaid, and I love her."

00:07:28.244 --> 00:07:30.105
He cried.

00:07:30.164 --> 00:07:34.256
It is horrible to love your body.

00:07:34.316 --> 00:07:35.916
cried the priest.

00:07:35.976 --> 00:07:40.618
The fawns of the woods and the mermaids are horrible.

00:07:40.677 --> 00:07:42.643
I hear them at night.

00:07:42.703 --> 00:07:46.260
They try to distract me from my prayers.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.291
They are lost, I tell you.

00:07:48.351 --> 00:07:49.692
They are lost.

00:07:49.751 --> 00:07:52.273
There is no heaven or hell for them.

00:07:52.293 --> 00:07:55.064
Away, away!"

00:07:55.124 --> 00:07:56.385
cried the priest.

00:07:56.445 --> 00:08:00.067
Your mermaid is lost and you will be lost with her.

00:08:00.127 --> 00:08:05.180
The young fisherman walked sadly to the marketplace.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:14.278
When the merchant saw him, they said, to himself, I will sell you my soul," he answered.

00:08:14.338 --> 00:08:18.522
Please buy it from me, because I am tired of it.

00:08:18.582 --> 00:08:20.814
What can I do with a soul?

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:23.196
I cannot see it.

00:08:23.256 --> 00:08:25.038
I cannot touch it.

00:08:25.097 --> 00:08:27.218
I do not know it.

00:08:27.278 --> 00:08:34.112
But the merchants laughed at him and said, What can we do with a soul?

00:08:34.132 --> 00:08:37.194
A false coin is more precious.

00:08:37.254 --> 00:08:41.797
Sellers your body, and we will give you a lot of gold.

00:08:41.857 --> 00:08:44.979
But we will not give you any money for your soul.

00:08:44.999 --> 00:08:47.411
The young fisherman thought.

00:08:47.471 --> 00:08:49.792
How strange this is.

00:08:49.852 --> 00:08:56.296
The priest said, your soul is as precious as all the gold in the world.

00:08:56.356 --> 00:09:01.449
But the merchants say, a false coin is more precious.

00:09:01.509 --> 00:09:07.450
He went to the beach and began to think.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:18.704
Chapter 2 The Witch At midday, he remembered that there was a young witch.

00:09:18.764 --> 00:09:23.406
She lived in a cave and she was very good at magic.

00:09:23.466 --> 00:09:26.458
He ran quickly to her.

00:09:26.518 --> 00:09:28.548
What do you need?

00:09:28.608 --> 00:09:30.058
What do you need?

00:09:30.118 --> 00:09:31.360
She cried.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.953
when he ran towards her cave.

00:09:34.013 --> 00:09:37.494
Do you need fish when the weather is bad?

00:09:37.554 --> 00:09:40.105
I have a special instrument.

00:09:40.165 --> 00:09:44.607
You play it and all the fish swim into the bay.

00:09:44.667 --> 00:09:46.658
But it has a price.

00:09:46.718 --> 00:09:48.308
Pretty boy.

00:09:48.368 --> 00:09:50.940
It has a price.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.200
What do you need?

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.371
What do you need?

00:09:54.391 --> 00:09:57.542
A storm to destroy the ships.

00:09:57.602 --> 00:10:00.934
Do you want the gold on the ships?

00:10:00.994 --> 00:10:03.098
I can help you.

00:10:03.158 --> 00:10:06.480
I have more storms than the wind.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:12.934
My master is stronger than the wind, but I have a price, pretty boy.

00:10:12.994 --> 00:10:14.886
I have a price."

00:10:14.945 --> 00:10:18.858
I do not want very much, said the young fisherman.

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:24.742
But the priest is very angry with me, and the merchants laugh at me.

00:10:24.802 --> 00:10:30.218
So I came to you, and I will pay you any price.

00:10:30.278 --> 00:10:32.260
What do you want?"

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.161
asked the witch.

00:10:34.221 --> 00:10:40.254
I want to send my soul away from me, answered the young fisherman.

00:10:40.315 --> 00:10:43.936
The witch's face became white.

00:10:43.996 --> 00:10:48.970
Pretty boy, pretty boy, she said.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:52.904
That is a terrible thing to do.

00:10:52.964 --> 00:10:57.060
He laughed and answered her.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:01.043
My soul is not important to me.

00:11:01.103 --> 00:11:02.954
I cannot see it.

00:11:03.014 --> 00:11:04.866
I cannot touch it.

00:11:04.926 --> 00:11:07.558
I do not know it.

00:11:07.618 --> 00:11:15.298
I will tell you, but you must give me something, said the witch.

00:11:15.358 --> 00:11:19.706
She looked at him with her beautiful eyes.

00:11:19.766 --> 00:11:27.700
Five pieces of gold, he said, and my nets, and my house, and my boat.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.752
But how can I send away my soul?

00:11:30.812 --> 00:11:33.813
She laughed and answered.

00:11:33.873 --> 00:11:38.105
I can change the autumn leaves into gold.

00:11:38.165 --> 00:11:42.462
I can change the light of the moon into silver.

00:11:42.522 --> 00:11:47.989
My master is richer than all the kings of this world.

00:11:48.049 --> 00:11:53.290
The witch caressed his hair with her thin white hand.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:57.821
You must dance with me, pretty boy.

00:11:57.881 --> 00:12:00.011
She said softly.

00:12:00.071 --> 00:12:02.472
And she smiled at him.

00:12:02.532 --> 00:12:03.902
Only this?

00:12:03.962 --> 00:12:06.502
Cried the young fisherman.

00:12:06.562 --> 00:12:10.622
Only this, she answered.

00:12:10.682 --> 00:12:13.163
And she smiled at him again.

00:12:13.223 --> 00:12:18.405
Then we will dance together in a secret place at sunset.

00:12:18.465 --> 00:12:19.365
He said.

00:12:19.425 --> 00:12:22.206
And you will tell me everything.

00:12:22.266 --> 00:12:25.937
Then I can send away my soul.

00:12:25.997 --> 00:12:28.428
When the moon is full.

00:12:28.488 --> 00:12:31.219
When the moon is full.

00:12:31.279 --> 00:12:33.410
She said softly.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.981
Then she looked around and listened.

00:12:37.041 --> 00:12:39.334
Three birds sang.

00:12:39.394 --> 00:12:42.167
There was no other sound.

00:12:42.227 --> 00:12:45.889
There was only the sound of the waves.

00:12:45.949 --> 00:12:48.740
So she pulled him next to her.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:52.932
She put her dry lips close to his ear.

00:12:52.992 --> 00:12:59.736
Tonight, you must come to the top of the mountain, she whispered.

00:12:59.796 --> 00:13:04.998
It is a special night, and he will be there.

00:13:05.058 --> 00:13:07.459
Who is he?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.179
He asked.

00:13:09.239 --> 00:13:13.569
It is not important," she answered.

00:13:13.629 --> 00:13:19.840
Go to night and stand under the tree and wait for me.

00:13:19.901 --> 00:13:25.442
You will see a dog and you must hit it with a stick.

00:13:25.502 --> 00:13:28.482
The dog will run away.

00:13:28.542 --> 00:13:33.104
Remember, do not speak to the owl.

00:13:33.164 --> 00:13:39.706
I will come with the full moon and we will dance together.

00:13:39.766 --> 00:13:43.139
How can I send my soul away?

00:13:43.199 --> 00:13:45.591
You must promise to tell me."

00:13:45.651 --> 00:13:47.243
He said.

00:13:47.302 --> 00:13:51.706
She came out of the cave into the sun.

00:13:51.766 --> 00:13:55.690
I promise, she answered.

00:13:55.750 --> 00:14:04.266
You are the best witch in the world, cried the fisherman, and he ran back to the town happily.

00:14:04.326 --> 00:14:09.848
The witch went into her cave and burned a magic plant.

00:14:09.908 --> 00:14:12.656
She looked into the smoke.

00:14:12.716 --> 00:14:18.387
After some time, she said angrily, he must be mine.

00:14:18.407 --> 00:14:22.018
I am as beautiful as she is.

00:14:22.078 --> 00:14:29.330
That evening, when the moon appeared, the fisherman went to the top of the mountain.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:32.080
He stood under the tree.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:36.482
A big owl with yellow eyes called his name.

00:14:36.542 --> 00:14:38.672
He did not answer.

00:14:38.732 --> 00:14:41.973
A black dog ran towards him.

00:14:42.033 --> 00:14:46.284
He hit it with a stick, and it ran away.

00:14:46.344 --> 00:14:50.314
At midnight, the witches were in the sky.

00:14:50.374 --> 00:14:54.455
They were like bats.

00:14:54.515 --> 00:14:57.536
They cried when they came to the ground.

00:14:57.596 --> 00:15:02.874
There is someone here, and we do not know him.

00:15:02.934 --> 00:15:07.445
Finally the young witch with red hair appeared.

00:15:07.505 --> 00:15:14.150
She wore a gold dress with peacock's eyes on it and her little hat was green.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.112
Where is he?

00:15:16.172 --> 00:15:17.974
Where is he?

00:15:18.034 --> 00:15:21.216
asked the witches when they saw her.

00:15:21.276 --> 00:15:24.678
She laughed and ran to the fisherman.

00:15:24.738 --> 00:15:29.792
She took him by the hand and then they danced in the moonlight.

00:15:29.852 --> 00:15:32.661
They danced round and round.

00:15:32.721 --> 00:15:36.400
Then they heard the sound of a galloping horse.

00:15:36.459 --> 00:15:38.921
But they did not see a horse.

00:15:38.981 --> 00:15:41.412
Faster, faster!"

00:15:41.472 --> 00:15:45.566
she cried, and then the fisherman was afraid.

00:15:45.626 --> 00:15:50.918
Something very bad was there, and he was afraid of it.

00:15:50.978 --> 00:15:54.361
There was a man near a rock.

00:15:54.421 --> 00:15:57.716
He wore elegant Spanish clothes.

00:15:57.776 --> 00:16:01.980
This man watched the fisherman constantly.

00:16:02.041 --> 00:16:10.256
The witch laughed and he danced with her round and round.

00:16:10.316 --> 00:16:23.195
Chapter 3 The Secret A dog barked and the dancers stopped.

00:16:23.254 --> 00:16:28.311
They went to the man and kissed his hand.

00:16:28.371 --> 00:16:32.276
Come, let's pray."

00:16:32.336 --> 00:16:35.108
The witch said softly.

00:16:35.168 --> 00:16:39.842
The fisherman wanted to do this, and he followed her.

00:16:39.902 --> 00:16:45.174
But when he came near the man, he called God's name.

00:16:45.234 --> 00:16:50.427
When he did this, the witches screamed and went away.

00:16:50.447 --> 00:16:55.534
A horse came, and the man got on it.

00:16:55.594 --> 00:17:01.824
He looked at the fisherman sadly, and then disappeared.

00:17:01.884 --> 00:17:09.695
The witch with red hair tried to fly away too, but the fisherman stopped her.

00:17:09.755 --> 00:17:11.277
Let me go!

00:17:11.297 --> 00:17:12.836
She cried.

00:17:12.897 --> 00:17:16.297
You must not say God's name.

00:17:16.357 --> 00:17:17.268
No.

00:17:17.328 --> 00:17:18.479
He answered.

00:17:18.539 --> 00:17:20.281
You are my prisoner.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.392
Tell me the secret now.

00:17:22.452 --> 00:17:24.143
What secret?

00:17:24.204 --> 00:17:25.854
Said the witch.

00:17:25.915 --> 00:17:27.936
She tried to escape.

00:17:27.996 --> 00:17:29.998
You know.

00:17:30.058 --> 00:17:32.380
He answered.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:41.166
She began to cry and said to the fisherman, ask me anything but not that.

00:17:41.226 --> 00:17:42.840
He laughed.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:45.454
and didn't want to release her.

00:17:45.514 --> 00:17:52.737
She could not escape, and so she said, I am as beautiful as the mermaids.

00:17:52.797 --> 00:17:56.138
And she put her face near his.

00:17:56.198 --> 00:18:00.290
But he pushed her away and said, I will kill you.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.331
You must tell me the secret now.

00:18:03.391 --> 00:18:04.972
She trembled.

00:18:05.032 --> 00:18:08.294
All right, she said.

00:18:08.354 --> 00:18:12.920
It is your soul, not mine.

00:18:12.981 --> 00:18:16.257
She gave him a little knife.

00:18:16.317 --> 00:18:18.898
Why did you give me this knife?

00:18:18.958 --> 00:18:20.608
He asked.

00:18:20.668 --> 00:18:23.299
She was silent for a moment.

00:18:23.359 --> 00:18:25.170
She was terrified.

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:31.872
Then she said to him, Our shadow is not the shadow of our bodies.

00:18:31.932 --> 00:18:35.313
It is the body of our souls.

00:18:35.373 --> 00:18:39.624
Stand on the beach with your back to the moon.

00:18:39.684 --> 00:18:42.601
Cut your shadow from your feet.

00:18:42.661 --> 00:18:48.890
Then you must tell your soul to leave, and it will leave.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:52.031
The young fisherman trembled.

00:18:52.091 --> 00:18:53.471
Is this true?

00:18:53.532 --> 00:18:54.712
He said.

00:18:54.772 --> 00:18:58.213
He released her and took the knife.

00:18:58.274 --> 00:19:01.245
Then he walked to the sea.

00:19:01.305 --> 00:19:06.978
The fisherman's soul then said to him, I am your servant.

00:19:07.038 --> 00:19:10.108
Do not send me away now.

00:19:10.168 --> 00:19:13.498
Did I do anything bad to you?

00:19:13.558 --> 00:19:17.439
The young fisherman laughed.

00:19:17.499 --> 00:19:21.932
You didn't do anything bad, but I do not need you.

00:19:21.992 --> 00:19:22.902
He answered.

00:19:22.962 --> 00:19:24.583
The world is big.

00:19:24.643 --> 00:19:31.367
Go where you want, but do not disturb me, because my love is calling me.

00:19:31.427 --> 00:19:36.350
His soul called him many times, but he did not listen.

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:42.108
He then arrived on the beach and stood on the sand with his back to the moon.

00:19:42.168 --> 00:19:47.654
White arms came out of the foam and they asked him to come.

00:19:47.714 --> 00:19:53.708
His soul said to him, Do not send me away without a heart.

00:19:53.768 --> 00:19:56.519
The world is cruel.

00:19:56.579 --> 00:19:59.170
Give me your heart.

00:19:59.231 --> 00:20:02.932
How can I love my mermaid without a heart?

00:20:02.992 --> 00:20:04.003
He cried.

00:20:04.063 --> 00:20:05.314
Please.

00:20:05.374 --> 00:20:06.934
Said his soul.

00:20:06.994 --> 00:20:08.785
Give me your heart.

00:20:08.845 --> 00:20:12.824
The world is cruel and I am afraid.

00:20:12.884 --> 00:20:15.762
My heart is with my love now."

00:20:15.822 --> 00:20:17.113
He answered.

00:20:17.173 --> 00:20:18.534
Go away.

00:20:18.594 --> 00:20:21.385
But I also need to love.

00:20:21.445 --> 00:20:22.956
Said his soul.

00:20:23.016 --> 00:20:24.346
Go away.

00:20:24.406 --> 00:20:26.247
I do not need you.

00:20:26.307 --> 00:20:28.218
Cried the young fisherman.

00:20:28.278 --> 00:20:32.770
He took the little knife and cut his shadow from his feet.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:38.720
The shadow stood up in front of him and it was very similar to the fisherman.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:43.750
The fisherman moved back slowly, and he was afraid.

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:47.942
Go away, he murmured, and never come back again.

00:20:47.962 --> 00:20:51.604
No, but we must meet again.

00:20:51.664 --> 00:20:53.154
Said the soul.

00:20:53.214 --> 00:20:56.396
The soul's voice was like a flute.

00:20:56.456 --> 00:20:58.357
How will we meet?

00:20:58.417 --> 00:21:00.208
Cried the young fisherman.

00:21:00.268 --> 00:21:02.800
Will you follow me into the sea?

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:08.051
Once every year I will come to this place and call you.

00:21:08.111 --> 00:21:09.490
said the soul.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:12.471
Perhaps you will need me.

00:21:12.531 --> 00:21:14.762
I do not think I will need you.

00:21:14.822 --> 00:21:16.362
Cried the young fisherman.

00:21:16.422 --> 00:21:18.172
But you can call me.

00:21:18.232 --> 00:21:20.433
I can come here again.

00:21:20.493 --> 00:21:26.504
He went in to the water and the Tritons played their musical instruments.

00:21:26.564 --> 00:21:29.765
The little mermaid came to meet him.

00:21:29.825 --> 00:21:34.640
She put her arms around his neck and kissed him on the mouth.

00:21:34.701 --> 00:21:39.068
The soul stood on the beach and watched them.

00:21:39.128 --> 00:21:49.406
And when they disappeared into the sea, the fisherman's soul walked away and cried.

00:21:49.466 --> 00:21:52.880
Chapter 4.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:22:02.412
The soul's first journey After a year, the soul came down to the sea and called the young fisherman.

00:22:02.471 --> 00:22:06.948
He came out of the sea and said, Why do you call me?

00:22:07.008 --> 00:22:10.540
The soul answered, Come near her.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:15.413
I want to speak to you because I saw marvellous things.

00:22:15.473 --> 00:22:20.476
So he came nearer and sat in the water and listened.

00:22:20.536 --> 00:22:27.900
The soul said to him, When I left you, I went towards the east and traveled.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:31.514
Everything wise comes from the east.

00:22:31.574 --> 00:22:35.850
After six days I came to the land of the Tatas.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:41.074
One night I saw a fire in a camp of a company of merchants.

00:22:41.134 --> 00:22:46.248
I went to them, and the chief of merchants stood up and took his sword.

00:22:46.308 --> 00:22:47.849
Who are you?

00:22:47.909 --> 00:22:49.380
He asked.

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:53.834
I am a prince, and I escaped from the Tatas.

00:22:53.894 --> 00:22:55.644
I replied.

00:22:55.704 --> 00:23:00.812
He lowered his head as a sign of respect and took my hand.

00:23:00.872 --> 00:23:10.222
Then we left the country of the Tatas and we traveled in many strange lands and saw many strange people.

00:23:10.282 --> 00:23:14.436
I traveled on a camel next to the chief.

00:23:14.496 --> 00:23:20.121
There were forty camels in the caravan and eighty mules.

00:23:20.181 --> 00:23:25.235
During our journey we battled with the tribe of the Magadie.

00:23:25.295 --> 00:23:32.410
They are born old and grow younger every year and die when they are little children.

00:23:32.471 --> 00:23:35.232
We battled with the lactroi.

00:23:35.292 --> 00:23:41.356
They think they are the sons of tigers and they paint their bodies yellow and black.

00:23:41.416 --> 00:23:44.589
We also battled with the cibyans.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:50.392
They have horses feet and they run quicker than horses.

00:23:50.452 --> 00:23:55.813
In the fourth month we arrived in the city of Ilelle.

00:23:55.873 --> 00:23:59.924
It was night, and we waited for day to come.

00:23:59.984 --> 00:24:04.336
That morning we knocked at the gate of the city.

00:24:04.396 --> 00:24:12.728
The gate was of red bronze, and it had images of sea dragons and dragons with wings.

00:24:12.788 --> 00:24:17.483
A guard then said to us, What do you want?

00:24:17.543 --> 00:24:24.239
We are from the island of Syria, and we have a lot of merchandise to sell," we answered.

00:24:24.299 --> 00:24:26.940
Then wait here until midday!

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.351
He said.

00:24:28.411 --> 00:24:35.034
At midday they opened the gates, and we went to the marketplace.

00:24:35.094 --> 00:24:40.976
After a month in the city of Ilel, I became tired of it.

00:24:41.036 --> 00:24:47.135
I walked in the streets of the city, and came to the garden of the God of the city.

00:24:47.195 --> 00:24:52.764
The priests and their yellow tunics walked silently in the garden.

00:24:52.825 --> 00:24:55.286
There was a red house.

00:24:55.346 --> 00:24:58.128
This was the home of the God.

00:24:58.188 --> 00:25:04.092
The doors had images of golden animals and peacocks on them.

00:25:04.152 --> 00:25:08.764
There was a pool of clear water in front of the temple.

00:25:08.824 --> 00:25:11.286
I sat down near it.

00:25:11.346 --> 00:25:16.040
One of the priests came to me and stood behind me.

00:25:16.100 --> 00:25:18.083
What do you want?"

00:25:18.143 --> 00:25:19.943
he asked me.

00:25:20.004 --> 00:25:24.716
I want to see the God, I replied.

00:25:24.777 --> 00:25:31.710
The God is hunting in a forest, said the priest, and he looked at me strangely.

00:25:31.770 --> 00:25:34.402
Which forest is he in?

00:25:34.462 --> 00:25:39.104
Tell me, and I will go there, I answered.

00:25:39.164 --> 00:25:42.996
He moved his hands on his soft tunic.

00:25:43.056 --> 00:25:45.278
The God is asleep.

00:25:45.338 --> 00:25:46.845
He murmured.

00:25:46.905 --> 00:25:49.023
Which bed does he in?

00:25:49.083 --> 00:25:52.116
Tell me, and I will stand near him."

00:25:52.176 --> 00:25:53.226
I answered.

00:25:53.286 --> 00:25:56.078
The god is at the feast, he cried.

00:25:56.138 --> 00:26:01.152
I will drink bitter or sweet wine with him, I said.

00:26:01.212 --> 00:26:06.136
He was surprised and accompanied me into the temple.

00:26:06.196 --> 00:26:13.982
In the first room, I saw an ebony idol on a throne, and it was the size of a man.

00:26:14.042 --> 00:26:16.904
There was a ruby on its forehead.

00:26:16.964 --> 00:26:21.647
Its feet were red from the blood of a baby goat.

00:26:21.708 --> 00:26:26.819
I said to the priest, is this the God?

00:26:26.880 --> 00:26:30.832
This is the God, he answered.

00:26:30.892 --> 00:26:33.663
This is not the God.

00:26:33.723 --> 00:26:38.666
Show me the God, I cried, or I will kill you.

00:26:38.726 --> 00:26:43.731
I touched his hand, and it became small and dry.

00:26:43.792 --> 00:26:48.896
Make my hand better, and I will show you the God," he cried.

00:26:48.956 --> 00:26:53.708
So I breathed on his hand, and it became better.

00:26:53.768 --> 00:26:58.570
He trembled, and accompanied me into the second room.

00:26:58.630 --> 00:27:05.492
I saw an ivory idol on a lotus of jade with great emeralds on it.

00:27:05.552 --> 00:27:10.199
This idol was twice as big as a man.

00:27:10.259 --> 00:27:12.706
Is this the God?"

00:27:12.766 --> 00:27:14.226
I asked him.

00:27:14.286 --> 00:27:17.928
This is the God, he replied.

00:27:17.988 --> 00:27:20.530
This is not the God.

00:27:20.590 --> 00:27:25.332
Show me the God, I cried, or I will kill you.

00:27:25.393 --> 00:27:30.166
I touched his eyes, and they became blind.

00:27:30.226 --> 00:27:32.786
Please make my eyes better.

00:27:32.846 --> 00:27:36.928
Then I will show you the God, he cried.

00:27:36.988 --> 00:27:41.533
So I breathed on his eyes, and they could see again.

00:27:41.593 --> 00:27:47.089
The priest trembled and accompanied me into the third room.

00:27:47.149 --> 00:27:52.574
There was not an idol in it, only a mirror.

00:27:52.634 --> 00:27:57.618
I said to the priest, where is the God?

00:27:57.678 --> 00:28:05.324
He answered me, there is no God, but this is the mirror of wisdom.

00:28:05.384 --> 00:28:09.906
It reflects all the things in heaven and on earth.

00:28:09.966 --> 00:28:15.188
but it does not reflect the face of the person if they look into it.

00:28:15.248 --> 00:28:19.270
So, this person can become wise.

00:28:19.330 --> 00:28:24.564
There are many other mirrors, but they are mirrors of opinion.

00:28:24.624 --> 00:28:28.886
This is the only mirror of wisdom.

00:28:28.946 --> 00:28:33.479
When you possess this mirror, you know everything.

00:28:33.539 --> 00:28:39.504
So, it is a God, and we pray to this God.

00:28:39.564 --> 00:28:42.738
I looked into the mirror.

00:28:42.798 --> 00:28:46.328
The priest didn't lie.

00:28:46.388 --> 00:28:51.620
Then I did something strange, but it is not important.

00:28:51.680 --> 00:28:55.220
I placed the mirror in a valley near here.

00:28:55.280 --> 00:28:58.521
We can walk there in three days.

00:28:58.581 --> 00:29:04.692
Let me enter you again and be your servant, and you will have wisdom.

00:29:04.752 --> 00:29:08.004
But the young fisherman laughed.

00:29:08.064 --> 00:29:11.316
Love is better than wisdom.

00:29:11.376 --> 00:29:12.246
He cried.

00:29:12.306 --> 00:29:14.517
And the little mermaid loves me.

00:29:14.577 --> 00:29:15.617
No.

00:29:15.678 --> 00:29:18.578
There is nothing better than wisdom.

00:29:18.638 --> 00:29:20.089
Said the soul.

00:29:20.149 --> 00:29:22.030
Love is better.

00:29:22.090 --> 00:29:24.030
Answered the young fisherman.

00:29:24.090 --> 00:29:31.453
He went back to the sea, and the soul walked away and cried.

00:29:31.513 --> 00:29:45.430
Chapter 5 The Ring of Riches After the second year, the soul came down to the sea and called the young fisherman.

00:29:45.490 --> 00:29:49.641
He came out of the sea and said, Why do you call me?

00:29:49.701 --> 00:29:58.325
The soul answered, Come nearer, I want to speak to you, because I saw marvellous things.

00:29:58.385 --> 00:30:03.817
So he came nearer and sat in the water and listened.

00:30:03.877 --> 00:30:12.019
The soul said to him, When I left you, I went towards the south and traveled.

00:30:12.078 --> 00:30:16.643
Everything precious comes from the south.

00:30:16.703 --> 00:30:20.997
I traveled six days to the city of Ashta.

00:30:21.057 --> 00:30:25.812
I saw the city on the morning of the seventh day.

00:30:25.872 --> 00:30:28.414
The city is like a bazaar.

00:30:28.474 --> 00:30:30.099
It is wonderful.

00:30:30.159 --> 00:30:33.515
Merchants sit on silk carpets.

00:30:33.575 --> 00:30:42.452
Some of them sell strange perfumes from the islands of the Indian Sea and the oil of red roses.

00:30:42.512 --> 00:30:52.358
Other merchants sell fantastic jewelry with tiger claws in gold and leopard claws in gold also.

00:30:52.418 --> 00:30:56.048
The people sell all kinds of fruit.

00:30:56.108 --> 00:31:06.287
Purple things, yellow melons, white grapes, red gold oranges and oval lemons of green gold.

00:31:06.347 --> 00:31:08.397
I saw an elephant.

00:31:08.457 --> 00:31:13.458
It stopped and began eating the oranges and the people laughed.

00:31:13.519 --> 00:31:17.470
You cannot imagine how strange these people are.

00:31:17.530 --> 00:31:21.371
When they are happy, they buy a bird in a cage.

00:31:21.431 --> 00:31:26.150
Then they release the bird because they want to be happier.

00:31:26.210 --> 00:31:33.180
When they are sad, they hit their bodies with thorns because they want to be sadder.

00:31:33.240 --> 00:31:41.664
On the feast of the new moon, the emperor came out of his palace and went into the mosque to pray.

00:31:41.724 --> 00:31:47.652
The people covered their faces, but eyes showed him no form of respect.

00:31:47.712 --> 00:31:52.060
That night, the guards of the emperor came for me.

00:31:52.120 --> 00:31:54.981
They accompanied me into the palace.

00:31:55.040 --> 00:32:00.542
We walked across a great court, and then we entered a beautiful garden.

00:32:00.602 --> 00:32:04.554
At the end of the garden, there was a pavilion.

00:32:04.614 --> 00:32:08.738
Then the captain of the guard told me to enter.

00:32:08.798 --> 00:32:16.155
The young Emperor was there, on a bed of lion skins, and he held a falcon.

00:32:16.215 --> 00:32:19.106
A newbian stood behind him.

00:32:19.166 --> 00:32:25.130
A large scimitar of steel was on a table next to the bed.

00:32:25.190 --> 00:32:31.492
When the Emperor saw me, he was worried and said to me, What is your name?

00:32:31.552 --> 00:32:35.174
Don't you know that I am Emperor of this city?

00:32:35.234 --> 00:32:37.523
I did not answer him.

00:32:37.583 --> 00:32:45.358
He indicated the scimitar, and the Nubian took it and hit me with great violence.

00:32:45.418 --> 00:32:48.001
It did not hurt me.

00:32:48.061 --> 00:32:52.385
The Nubian was terrified and went away.

00:32:52.445 --> 00:32:57.490
The emperor tried to kill me with a lance, but he did not hurt me.

00:32:57.550 --> 00:33:02.824
He tried to kill me with an arrow, but I stopped it in the air.

00:33:02.884 --> 00:33:06.947
Then the emperor said to me, Why can't I hurt you?

00:33:07.007 --> 00:33:08.668
Are you a prophet?

00:33:08.729 --> 00:33:10.870
Or the son of a prophet?

00:33:10.930 --> 00:33:13.913
Please leave my city tonight.

00:33:13.973 --> 00:33:17.946
You are here now, and I am not its lord.

00:33:18.006 --> 00:33:19.748
I answered him.

00:33:19.808 --> 00:33:22.221
Give me half of your treasure.

00:33:22.280 --> 00:33:25.022
Then I will go away.

00:33:25.082 --> 00:33:30.778
So, he took my hand and accompanied me to a large room.

00:33:30.838 --> 00:33:34.192
He touched one of the walls and it opened.

00:33:34.252 --> 00:33:37.384
Then we walked down a corridor.

00:33:37.444 --> 00:33:42.530
He said a magic word and a granite door opened.

00:33:42.590 --> 00:33:50.126
The emperor covered his eyes with his hands to protect them from the light of the jewels there.

00:33:50.186 --> 00:33:53.298
It was really marvellous inside.

00:33:53.358 --> 00:34:00.984
There were huge tortoise shells full of pearls, and many other wonderful jewels.

00:34:01.044 --> 00:34:08.731
Then the emperor said to me, This is my house of treasure, and half of it is yours.

00:34:08.790 --> 00:34:10.912
But you must go to night.

00:34:10.973 --> 00:34:14.416
My father, the son, must not see this.

00:34:14.476 --> 00:34:17.509
I cannot kill a man in the city.

00:34:17.569 --> 00:34:19.600
I answered him.

00:34:19.660 --> 00:34:24.092
The gold and all the precious jewels are yours.

00:34:24.152 --> 00:34:28.664
I only want your little ring."

00:34:28.724 --> 00:34:31.394
The emperor frowned.

00:34:31.455 --> 00:34:36.103
It is only a ring of lead, he cried, and it has no value.

00:34:36.163 --> 00:34:40.333
Take your half of the treasure and go away from my city."

00:34:40.394 --> 00:34:42.695
No, I answered.

00:34:42.756 --> 00:34:48.481
I know that it is really the ring of riches.

00:34:48.540 --> 00:34:54.226
The emperor trembled and said, take all the treasure and go from my city.

00:34:54.286 --> 00:34:57.378
You can also have my half of the treasure.

00:34:57.438 --> 00:35:02.358
Then I did something strange, but it is not important.

00:35:02.418 --> 00:35:07.946
What is important is that I put the ring of riches in a cave.

00:35:08.006 --> 00:35:11.397
You can arrive there in one day.

00:35:11.457 --> 00:35:17.190
The owner of this ring is richer than all the kings of the world.

00:35:17.250 --> 00:35:20.862
But the young fisherman laughed.

00:35:20.922 --> 00:35:24.143
Love is better than riches.

00:35:24.203 --> 00:35:25.054
He cried.

00:35:25.114 --> 00:35:27.625
And the little mermaid loves me.

00:35:27.685 --> 00:35:31.346
No, nothing is better than riches.

00:35:31.406 --> 00:35:32.980
Said the soul.

00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:35.254
Love is better."

00:35:35.314 --> 00:35:38.107
answered the young fisherman.

00:35:38.167 --> 00:35:46.914
He went back to the sea, and the soul walked away and cried.

00:35:46.974 --> 00:36:00.692
Chapter 6 The soul's Third Journey After the third year, the soul came down to the sea and called the young fisherman.

00:36:00.752 --> 00:36:04.980
He came out of the sea and said, why do you call me?

00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:09.052
The soul answered, come near her.

00:36:09.112 --> 00:36:14.154
I want to speak to you because I saw marvellous things.

00:36:14.214 --> 00:36:19.306
So he came nearer and sat in the water and listened.

00:36:19.366 --> 00:36:25.679
The soul said to him, I went to an inn near a river in a city.

00:36:25.739 --> 00:36:30.274
I sat with sailors and they ordered food and drink.

00:36:30.334 --> 00:36:36.341
After some time, an old man entered with a carpet and a loot.

00:36:36.401 --> 00:36:39.262
He put the carpet on the floor.

00:36:39.322 --> 00:36:45.186
When he played the loot, a girl came in and began to dance.

00:36:45.246 --> 00:36:49.878
There was a veil on her face and she had no shoes.

00:36:49.938 --> 00:36:55.010
Her feet moved on the carpet like little white pigeons.

00:36:55.070 --> 00:37:00.041
It was really marvellous and it is only one day away from here.

00:37:00.101 --> 00:37:03.250
The young fisherman heard these words.

00:37:03.310 --> 00:37:08.404
He remembered that the little mermaid had no feet and could not dance.

00:37:08.464 --> 00:37:14.728
He thought, it is only one day away, and I can return to my love.

00:37:14.788 --> 00:37:19.830
He laughed, stood up in the water and walked towards the beach.

00:37:19.890 --> 00:37:25.624
When he reached the beach, his soul ran towards him and entered him.

00:37:25.684 --> 00:37:32.766
Then the young fisherman saw on the sand, the shadow of the body, the body of the soul.

00:37:32.826 --> 00:37:38.607
They began their journey and the next evening they came to a city.

00:37:38.667 --> 00:37:43.558
The young fisherman said to his soul, Does she dance in this city?

00:37:43.618 --> 00:37:45.408
His soul answered him.

00:37:45.468 --> 00:37:48.329
Not in this city, but another.

00:37:48.389 --> 00:37:51.129
Let's enter this city anyway.

00:37:51.189 --> 00:37:54.964
So they entered and walked in the streets.

00:37:55.024 --> 00:38:00.522
The young fisherman saw a silver cup on a stall in the street of the jewelers.

00:38:00.582 --> 00:38:05.565
His soul said to him, Take that silver cup and hide it.

00:38:05.625 --> 00:38:08.837
So he took the silver cup and hid it.

00:38:08.897 --> 00:38:11.898
And they went quickly out of the city.

00:38:11.958 --> 00:38:17.232
When they were far from the city, the young fisherman threw the cup away.

00:38:17.292 --> 00:38:22.526
He said to his soul, It was not a good thing to take the cup and hide it.

00:38:22.587 --> 00:38:24.408
But his soul answered him.

00:38:24.468 --> 00:38:25.829
Calm down.

00:38:25.889 --> 00:38:27.449
Calm down.

00:38:27.510 --> 00:38:31.951
On the evening of the second day, they came to a city.

00:38:32.011 --> 00:38:34.942
The young fisherman said to his soul.

00:38:35.002 --> 00:38:37.412
Does she dance in this city?

00:38:37.472 --> 00:38:39.343
His soul answered him.

00:38:39.403 --> 00:38:42.434
Not in this city, but in another.

00:38:42.494 --> 00:38:45.145
Let's enter this city anyway.

00:38:45.205 --> 00:38:48.804
So they entered and walked in the streets.

00:38:48.864 --> 00:38:54.313
In the street of the cellars of sandals, the young fisherman saw a child.

00:38:54.373 --> 00:38:57.814
His soul said to him, hit that child.

00:38:57.874 --> 00:39:04.567
So he hit the child, and the child cried, and then they went quickly out of the city.

00:39:04.627 --> 00:39:13.940
When they were far from the city, the young fisherman became angry and said to his soul, it was not a good thing to hit the child.

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:18.938
But his soul answered him, calm down, calm down.

00:39:18.998 --> 00:39:23.855
On the evening of the third day, they came to a city.

00:39:23.915 --> 00:39:26.926
The young fisherman said to his soul.

00:39:26.986 --> 00:39:29.436
Does she dance in this city?

00:39:29.496 --> 00:39:31.356
His soul answered him.

00:39:31.416 --> 00:39:34.217
Perhaps this is the city.

00:39:34.277 --> 00:39:35.978
Let's enter.

00:39:36.038 --> 00:39:42.169
They walked in the streets, but the young fisherman could not find the inn near the river.

00:39:42.229 --> 00:39:46.140
He wanted to leave, but his soul said to him.

00:39:46.200 --> 00:39:48.274
Let's stay here tonight.

00:39:48.334 --> 00:39:51.300
Perhaps there are robbers outside.

00:39:51.360 --> 00:39:55.202
So the fisherman sat down in the marketplace.

00:39:55.262 --> 00:39:59.365
After some time a merchant came and said to him.

00:39:59.425 --> 00:40:01.026
Why are you here?

00:40:01.086 --> 00:40:03.177
The market is closed.

00:40:03.237 --> 00:40:05.579
The young fisherman answered him.

00:40:05.639 --> 00:40:08.430
I can't find an inn in this city.

00:40:08.491 --> 00:40:12.463
I have no family here and I need a room for the night.

00:40:12.523 --> 00:40:15.085
We are all of the same family.

00:40:15.145 --> 00:40:16.326
Said the merchant.

00:40:16.386 --> 00:40:18.450
And one God made us.

00:40:18.510 --> 00:40:19.544
Come with me.

00:40:19.564 --> 00:40:21.724
I have a room."

00:40:21.784 --> 00:40:25.385
The young fisherman followed the merchant to his house.

00:40:25.445 --> 00:40:29.276
The merchant gave him good food and a comfortable room.

00:40:29.336 --> 00:40:32.266
The young fisherman then went to sleep.

00:40:32.326 --> 00:40:42.838
After three hours, his soul woke him and said, Go to the room of the merchant and kill him and take his gold.

00:40:42.898 --> 00:40:46.618
The young fisherman went into the merchant's room.

00:40:46.678 --> 00:40:52.872
There was a sword near his feet and nine purses of gold next to the bed.

00:40:52.932 --> 00:40:59.676
When he touched the sword, the merchant woke up and said, Why do you want to kill me?

00:40:59.736 --> 00:41:02.368
I gave you good food in a room.

00:41:02.428 --> 00:41:03.998
I was kind to you.

00:41:04.018 --> 00:41:08.641
His soul said to the young fisherman, Hit him.

00:41:08.702 --> 00:41:12.663
So he hit him and the merchant lost consciousness.

00:41:12.723 --> 00:41:18.337
He then took the nine purses of gold and went quickly away from the city.

00:41:18.398 --> 00:41:23.552
When they were far from the city, the young fisherman said to his soul.

00:41:23.612 --> 00:41:27.116
It was bad to hit the merchant and take his gold.

00:41:27.176 --> 00:41:29.438
But his soul answered him.

00:41:29.498 --> 00:41:31.110
Calm down.

00:41:31.170 --> 00:41:32.512
Calm down.

00:41:32.572 --> 00:41:33.342
No!

00:41:33.402 --> 00:41:34.893
cried the young fisherman.

00:41:34.953 --> 00:41:36.594
I cannot become.

00:41:36.654 --> 00:41:39.065
You told me to do bad things.

00:41:39.125 --> 00:41:40.996
And I hate these things.

00:41:41.056 --> 00:41:43.197
I also hate you.

00:41:43.258 --> 00:41:45.248
Why did you do these things?

00:41:45.308 --> 00:41:47.340
His soul answered him.

00:41:47.400 --> 00:41:53.042
When you sent me out into the world, you did not give me a heart.

00:41:53.102 --> 00:41:56.905
So I learned to do all these things and love them.

00:41:56.965 --> 00:41:58.916
What are you saying?

00:41:58.976 --> 00:42:00.936
Mermaid the young fisherman.

00:42:00.996 --> 00:42:04.078
You know answered his soul.

00:42:04.138 --> 00:42:06.740
You did not give me a hat.

00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:08.942
So stay calm.

00:42:09.002 --> 00:42:12.965
You will give other people all kinds of pain.

00:42:13.025 --> 00:42:16.708
And you will receive all kinds of pleasure.

00:42:16.768 --> 00:42:22.032
The young fisherman said to his soul, No, you are bad.

00:42:22.092 --> 00:42:27.116
And I forgot about my love and did many bad things because of you.

00:42:27.176 --> 00:42:29.071
His soul answered him.

00:42:29.131 --> 00:42:33.212
You did not forget that you sent me away without a heart.

00:42:33.272 --> 00:42:37.139
Let's go to another city and enjoy life together.

00:42:37.199 --> 00:42:40.275
We have nine purses of gold.

00:42:40.335 --> 00:42:46.530
But the young fisherman took the nine purses of gold and threw them on the ground.

00:42:46.591 --> 00:42:52.636
No, I will not come with you and I will send you away again," said the young fisherman.

00:42:52.696 --> 00:42:54.938
He turned his back to the moon.

00:42:54.998 --> 00:43:00.562
With the little knife he tried to cut his shadow from his feet to eliminate his soul.

00:43:00.622 --> 00:43:04.916
But his soul did not leave him and said to him.

00:43:04.976 --> 00:43:08.208
The magic of the witch will not work.

00:43:08.268 --> 00:43:12.732
It only works once in a man's life.

00:43:12.792 --> 00:43:15.774
I will stay with you forever.

00:43:15.834 --> 00:43:20.128
And this is your punishment and your recompense.

00:43:20.188 --> 00:43:26.462
Now the young fisherman was desperate and cried because his soul was very bad.

00:43:26.522 --> 00:43:33.499
When it was day, the young fisherman said to his soul, I will tie my hands together.

00:43:33.559 --> 00:43:37.058
Then I cannot do what you tell me to do.

00:43:37.118 --> 00:43:41.440
I will return to the bay because my love sings there.

00:43:41.500 --> 00:43:43.372
I will call her.

00:43:43.433 --> 00:43:49.170
I will tell her about the bad things I did and the bad things you did to me."

00:43:49.230 --> 00:43:54.796
When he arrived on the beach, he freed his hands and called the mermaid.

00:43:54.856 --> 00:43:56.994
But she did not come.

00:43:57.054 --> 00:44:04.814
His soul laughed at him and said, Your love gives you little joy.

00:44:04.874 --> 00:44:07.856
Come with me to the valley of pleasure.

00:44:07.916 --> 00:44:09.978
That is better for you.

00:44:10.038 --> 00:44:13.659
The young fisherman did not answer his soul.

00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:18.527
He built a house by the bay and lived there for a year.

00:44:18.588 --> 00:44:28.430
Every morning he called the mermaid and every midday he called her again and at night he spoke her name.

00:44:28.490 --> 00:44:34.696
But she never came to see him and he did not see her anywhere.

00:44:34.756 --> 00:44:48.310
His soul always asked him to do bad things but the young fisherman never listened to him because the power of his love was so great.

00:44:48.370 --> 00:45:03.830
Chapter 7 Love After another year, the soul thought, I tempted him with bad, and his love is stronger than I am.

00:45:03.890 --> 00:45:08.881
I will now tempt him with good, and perhaps he will come with me.

00:45:08.941 --> 00:45:18.426
So he spoke to the young fisherman and said, I told you about the joy of the world, and you did not listen to me.

00:45:18.486 --> 00:45:24.212
Now I will tell you about the pain in the world, and maybe you will listen.

00:45:24.272 --> 00:45:29.456
Pain is the Lord of this world, and nobody can escape it.

00:45:29.516 --> 00:45:36.270
Some people do not have clothes, and other people do not have food, and others are ill.

00:45:36.330 --> 00:45:40.352
Come, let's go and help these people.

00:45:40.412 --> 00:45:43.164
Why do you wait here for your love?

00:45:43.224 --> 00:45:44.914
What is love?

00:45:44.974 --> 00:45:47.400
Why do you think it is so important?

00:45:47.460 --> 00:45:50.506
But the young fisherman did not answer.

00:45:50.566 --> 00:45:53.848
The power of his love was so great.

00:45:53.908 --> 00:45:59.511
Every morning he called the mermaid, and every midday he called her again.

00:45:59.571 --> 00:46:02.502
And at night he spoke her name.

00:46:02.562 --> 00:46:05.224
But she never came to see him.

00:46:05.284 --> 00:46:08.766
And he did not see her anywhere.

00:46:08.826 --> 00:46:21.208
After the second year, the soul said to the fisherman, I tempted you with bad, and I tempted you with good, and your love is stronger than I am.

00:46:21.268 --> 00:46:28.678
So I will not tempt you any more, but can I please enter your heart and be with you again?"

00:46:28.738 --> 00:46:32.672
Of course you can enter, said the young fisherman.

00:46:32.732 --> 00:46:36.362
I am sure you suffered when you did not have a heart.

00:46:36.422 --> 00:46:42.825
But I can find no place to enter, because there is love all around your heart.

00:46:42.885 --> 00:46:44.976
There's no space for me."

00:46:45.036 --> 00:46:46.637
cried the soul.

00:46:46.697 --> 00:46:48.948
I am very sorry.

00:46:49.008 --> 00:46:51.299
said the young fisherman.

00:46:51.359 --> 00:46:59.842
Just then he heard a terrible cry of sadness from the sea.

00:46:59.902 --> 00:47:05.744
The young fisherman ran to the beach.

00:47:05.804 --> 00:47:09.165
The black waves came quickly to the beach.

00:47:09.226 --> 00:47:12.967
They carried something that was whiter than silver.

00:47:13.027 --> 00:47:19.489
There at his feet the young fisherman saw the dead body of the little mermaid.

00:47:19.550 --> 00:47:25.776
He sat down next to her and he kissed her cold red mouth.

00:47:25.836 --> 00:47:32.024
He told the dead mermaid about his soul, and all the bad things.

00:47:32.084 --> 00:47:39.729
He put her little hands around his neck, and he touched her neck with his fingers.

00:47:39.789 --> 00:47:46.583
His joy was bitter, and his pain was full of strange happiness.

00:47:46.644 --> 00:47:53.451
The Black Sea came nearer and nearer to them.

00:47:53.511 --> 00:47:58.906
The sea is coming closer and closer.

00:47:58.966 --> 00:48:00.277
Go away.

00:48:00.337 --> 00:48:01.947
It will kill you.

00:48:02.007 --> 00:48:04.358
Run away to a safe place.

00:48:04.418 --> 00:48:08.849
But please do not send me into another world without a heart.

00:48:08.909 --> 00:48:12.730
But the young fisherman did not listen to his soul.

00:48:12.790 --> 00:48:25.398
He said to the little mermaid, love is better than wisdom and more precious than riches and more beautiful than the feet of the daughters of men.

00:48:25.458 --> 00:48:30.404
I called you in the morning, but you did not come.

00:48:30.464 --> 00:48:36.166
The moon heard your name, but you did not listen to me.

00:48:36.226 --> 00:48:48.771
I was bad when I abandoned you, but your love was always with me, and it was always stronger than bad and good.

00:48:48.831 --> 00:48:54.876
And now that you are dead, I will die with you also.

00:48:54.936 --> 00:48:58.422
His soul implored him to leave.

00:48:58.482 --> 00:49:03.966
But his love was too great, and he did not listen to his soul.

00:49:04.026 --> 00:49:08.840
The sea came near and tried to cover him with its waves.

00:49:08.900 --> 00:49:17.978
When he knew that the end was near, the young fisherman kissed the cold lips of the mermaid and his heart broke.

00:49:18.038 --> 00:49:21.860
It broke because it was so full of love.

00:49:21.920 --> 00:49:25.582
Then the soul finally entered his heart.

00:49:25.642 --> 00:49:33.615
and the sea covered the young fisherman with its waves.

00:49:33.675 --> 00:49:52.086
Chapter 8 The Field of the Fullers In the morning the priest said, I will go and bless the sea because it was not calm last night.

00:49:52.147 --> 00:49:56.546
Monk's musicians and many other people went with him.

00:49:56.606 --> 00:50:01.856
When the priest reached the beach, he saw the young fisherman.

00:50:01.916 --> 00:50:08.208
He was dead in the water and the body of the little mermaid was in his arms.

00:50:08.268 --> 00:50:16.543
The priest frowned and said, I will not bless the sea or anything in the sea.

00:50:16.603 --> 00:50:26.853
The young fisherman abandoned God for love and the punishment of God killed him and his love.

00:50:26.913 --> 00:50:35.892
Now take his body and the body of the mermaid and bury them in the corner of the field of the fullers.

00:50:35.953 --> 00:50:39.495
Do not put any sign there.

00:50:39.555 --> 00:50:46.539
The people put the dead bodies in a deep hole in the corner of the field of the fullers.

00:50:46.599 --> 00:50:49.200
They covered the hole with earth.

00:50:49.261 --> 00:50:52.260
No sweet herbs grew there.

00:50:52.320 --> 00:51:01.494
Three years later on a holy day, the priest went to the chapel to speak to the people about the anger of God.

00:51:01.554 --> 00:51:07.860
When he went to the altar, he saw that there were strange flowers on the altar.

00:51:07.920 --> 00:51:13.474
Their strange beauty worried him, and their perfume was sweet.

00:51:13.534 --> 00:51:20.092
He was particularly happy, and he did not understand why he was so happy.

00:51:20.152 --> 00:51:31.302
He wanted to speak to them about the anger of God, but the beauty of the white flowers worried him, and their perfume was sweet.

00:51:31.362 --> 00:51:34.764
He did not speak of the anger of God.

00:51:34.824 --> 00:51:41.566
He spoke of the love of God, and he did not know why he spoke like this.

00:51:41.626 --> 00:51:48.546
When he finished speaking, the people cried, and his eyes were full of tears.

00:51:48.606 --> 00:51:56.588
He was in a dream, and he said to his deacons, What are the flowers on the altar?

00:51:56.648 --> 00:51:58.780
Where do they come from?

00:51:58.840 --> 00:52:00.620
They answered him.

00:52:00.681 --> 00:52:07.836
We do not know what kind of flowers they are, but they come from the corner of the field of the fullers.

00:52:07.897 --> 00:52:13.424
The priest trembled, and returned to his house and prayed.

00:52:13.484 --> 00:52:20.452
Early the next morning, he left his house with monks, musicians and many other people.

00:52:20.512 --> 00:52:28.128
He walked to the beach and blessed the sea, and all the wild things in it.

00:52:28.188 --> 00:52:34.154
He also blessed the forms and the little things that danced in the forest.

00:52:34.214 --> 00:52:40.400
He blessed all things in the world of God, and the people were full of joy.

00:52:40.460 --> 00:52:49.015
The people of the sea went to another part of the sea and they never came back again.

00:52:49.075 --> 00:52:58.090
The Little Mermaid The king of the sea had six daughters.

00:52:58.150 --> 00:53:03.142
The youngest daughter had a beautiful underwater garden.

00:53:03.202 --> 00:53:07.094
In the garden there was a marble statue.

00:53:07.154 --> 00:53:12.718
It was the statue of a handsome prince, and she loved it.

00:53:12.778 --> 00:53:24.848
One day, their grandmother said to the six mermaids, When you are fifteen years old, you can go to the surface and see the world of the mortals.

00:53:24.908 --> 00:53:30.232
The youngest mermaid wanted to be fifteen very much.

00:53:30.292 --> 00:53:35.976
Finally, her fifteenth birthday came and she went to the surface.

00:53:36.036 --> 00:53:39.079
She saw a beautiful ship.

00:53:39.139 --> 00:53:44.190
There was a birthday party on the ship for a handsome prince.

00:53:44.250 --> 00:53:50.202
But a great storm came and broke the ship into many pieces.

00:53:50.262 --> 00:53:54.024
The prince fell into the water.

00:53:54.084 --> 00:54:03.804
At first the mermaid was very happy, but then she remembered that human beings could not live under water.

00:54:03.864 --> 00:54:07.954
She took him to the beach and left him there.

00:54:08.014 --> 00:54:12.908
He did not know that the little mermaid saved his life.

00:54:12.968 --> 00:54:16.000
She returned to her home.

00:54:16.060 --> 00:54:26.038
She was only happy when she put her arms around the statue in her garden, and when she swam near the prince's castle by the sea.

00:54:26.098 --> 00:54:30.550
One day she asked her grandmother about humans.

00:54:30.610 --> 00:54:40.226
Her grandmother said, We live for three hundred years, but when we die we dissolve in the water and disappear.

00:54:40.286 --> 00:54:47.580
Humans do not live very long, but they have an immortal soul that lives forever.

00:54:47.640 --> 00:54:50.110
I want to be like them!"

00:54:50.170 --> 00:54:52.201
cried the little mermaid.

00:54:52.262 --> 00:54:57.454
When a human loves you, you can have an immortal soul.

00:54:57.514 --> 00:55:00.050
But that is impossible.

00:55:00.110 --> 00:55:04.258
We have tales, and they are very beautiful.

00:55:04.318 --> 00:55:07.610
But humans think they are ugly.

00:55:07.670 --> 00:55:15.406
Humans have two ugly things called legs, and they think they are beautiful.

00:55:15.466 --> 00:55:20.300
The little mermaid decided to go to the sea witch for help.

00:55:20.360 --> 00:55:25.154
The sea witch said, I know why you are here.

00:55:25.214 --> 00:55:28.186
I will give you a magic drink.

00:55:28.246 --> 00:55:30.206
You must drink it.

00:55:30.266 --> 00:55:34.875
And your tail will divide in two, and you will have legs.

00:55:34.936 --> 00:55:37.436
But you must pay me.

00:55:37.496 --> 00:55:41.348
You must give me your beautiful voice.

00:55:41.408 --> 00:55:45.590
Remember, the prince must marry you.

00:55:45.650 --> 00:55:52.942
If he marries another, you will dissolve in the water and disappear."

00:55:53.002 --> 00:55:59.130
The little mermaid drank the magic drink, and then she had legs.

00:55:59.190 --> 00:56:03.267
The prince saw her and took her into his castle.

00:56:03.327 --> 00:56:07.649
He liked her very much, but he did not want to marry her.

00:56:07.709 --> 00:56:13.012
In fact, after some time, he married a human princess.

00:56:13.072 --> 00:56:22.037
On the evening of the wedding, the mermaid thought, Tomorrow when the sun comes up, I will dissolve in the water.

00:56:22.097 --> 00:56:24.098
I will disappear.

00:56:24.158 --> 00:56:28.340
But the mermaid's sisters had a knife from the sea witch.

00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:34.664
They said, Kill the prince with this knife, and then you will have your tail again.

00:56:34.724 --> 00:56:39.896
You will live with us under the water for three hundred years."

00:56:39.956 --> 00:56:47.890
When the Little Mermaid saw the prince, she did not want to kill him, and she threw the knife into the sea.

00:56:47.950 --> 00:56:53.984
Just then the sun appeared in the sky, but she did not disappear.

00:56:54.044 --> 00:57:00.317
No, she went up into the sky, and she heard beautiful voices.

00:57:00.378 --> 00:57:04.590
They were the voices of the daughters of the air.

00:57:04.650 --> 00:57:21.882
They said to her, You must do good things for humans for three hundred years, and then you can have an immortal soul and be with God.

00:57:21.942 --> 00:57:28.129
Thank you.

